WEBVTT

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.610
Like this, Misato?

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:10.720
The line you make with your toes 
is a little off again.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.700
You gotta kick that habit, Watari.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.030
Sorry.

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.310
Your toes should be more like... this.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:20.790
Like this?

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.370
Yeah, much better.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:25.580
Yah!

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.990
Thanks a ton, Misato!

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:28.790
Don't mention it.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:34.410
Onagawa, your aerial posture for your 
salto layouts is way better than before.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:37.450
The fruits of my top-secret training!

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:40.100
You asked Misato-kun 
about that yesterday, right?

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:44.020
That's our little secret, Serious Leaf.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.410
Everyone's looking good.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:50.570
Yeah.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:21.990
<b><i>Backflip!!</i></b>

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.550
The regional tournament is in two days.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:27.110
You've all been working very hard.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.540
No practice tomorrow.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:33.110
Take the day to build up energy
for the competition.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:33.880
All right?

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.050
Yes, sir!

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:37.560
I know you can do this.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.570
Go in with confidence.

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:41.310
Asa-chan.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:43.800
I'll now review the schedule.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.850
The venue is Kesennuma's public gymnasium.

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:50.350
The opening ceremony will begin at 9:30,

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:52.520
so let's meet up at the entrance at 9:00.

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:55.860
Okay, everyone. Let's give it our best.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.010
Yes, sir!

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:58.940
By the way...

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:03.610
I've acquired footage 
of the competing schools.

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:04.870
Whoa!

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:09.880
Representing Iwate Prefecture... 
Morioka Ryooh High School.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.070
This must be their first appearance.

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:12.750
That's right.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:15.650
They're so polished.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:18.590
It'll be twelve schools in total, right?

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:19.810
Yes.

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:24.460
Two schools from each of Tohoku's
 six prefectures participate in regionals.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.810
The top two move on to the Inter-High.

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:31.950
One of the favorites is, 
of course, Shiro High.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:35.290
This was their prefectural 
tournament performance?

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:36.030
That's right.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:38.320
They sure ain't bad.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:40.000
Mashiro-kun...

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:42.950
The Inter-High will be even more competitive.

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:48.950
There are several other strong 
schools all across the country.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:53.900
There's Midorisawa Kofu High School 
from Saga Prefecture, known for their lifts.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:58.440
Kagoshima Shien Academy of Kagoshima, 
known for their unique choreography.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:02.550
And Kokuteiin High School of Tokyo, 
known for vying for the top

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:04.780
against Shiro High every year.

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:10.220
We have to get through regionals 
if we want to share the spotlight with them.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.410
We need to work hard.

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.280
But for tomorrow, rest.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:22.940
It's important to allow your body to recover.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.910
We know, Manager.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:31.280
It's a little late in the game 
to start panicking.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:34.290
Let's all have a nice, relaxing day off!

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.190
Yah!

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.040
Sounds good.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.690
How will you spend tomorrow, Captain?

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:44.050
Might pitch in for the family business.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.550
This is great timing!

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:49.470
I'd given up all hope of gettin' to see 
the Tan Tan Girls' mini-concert.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:53.640
And there's a screenin' of the new 
<i>Carnage of Honor</i>, I do believe.

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:57.570
What should the two of us do, then?

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:16.960
Huh? You guys are still here?

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:21.890
Onagawa-senpai, 
you'll be late to your concert.

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:23.120
Oh?

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:25.480
Yeah... I'm on my way.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.320
Just gonna finish this first.

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:34.770
Anything else to wash?

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:40.880
Captain, is it even your turn 
to wash dishes today?

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:43.730
Weren't you going to help
 at your family business?

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:47.840
Yeah... I thought about it, 
but they've probably got enough help.

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:51.900
They don't need me there.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:06.680
That rhythm... That's our performance track!

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:10.360
Captain!

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:12.860
You're just itchin' to practice, ain'tcha?!

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:16.060
N-No way... I just...

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:21.860
What about you, Onagawa?! 
Just look at your fingers!

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.150
You've got 'em locked together perfectly!

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:28.900
What?! Oh, crap!

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:32.480
Calm down, both of you!

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:34.630
Tsukidate!

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:36.820
You're just as bad as we are!

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.130
When did that happen?!

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:45.170
<b>Battles Without 
Morals 
and Humanity</b>

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:44.640
I wanna do it...

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:48.050
I wanna do it!

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:49.300
Watari-senpai?

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:54.470
I wanna do jumps! I wanna do backflips!

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:58.810
Wh-What should we do, Misato-kun?

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:02.480
I'm feeling a little restless myself.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.030
Get a grip, Shotaro!

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:06.880
The rest of you, too!

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:07.820
I know...

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:11.460
Let's find something to distract ourselves.

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:14.160
Captain, why don't you eat some sasakama?

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.560
I did!

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:17.040
110 Years in Business

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:17.040
<b>Sasa 
Kamaboko</b>

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:17.040
I already ate it all!

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:20.790
I can't even taste sasakama anymore!

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:25.290
I can't hear Ma-chan's voice anymore!

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:30.920
Sorry, Bunya! Your words 
no longer stir my heart!

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:34.930
My plants... My plants aren't
 talking to me anymore!

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:39.810
They've got it bad.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:43.070
I know! The dictionary!

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:44.830
Anyone want to read dictionaries?

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:47.150
Dictionaries?

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:50.500
I personally really like them.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:52.650
They're pretty interesting!

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:57.910
<b>Daitokai</b>

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:57.910
